      "text": "1. **Calculate the total number of ways Terry picks two candies:**\n\\[ 20 \\times 19 = 380 \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the probability that Terry picks two blue candies:**\n\\[ 10 \\times 9 = 90 \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the probability that the same two blue candies are both picked by Terry and Mary:**\n\\[ \\frac{90}{380} \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the probability that Terry picks two red candies:**\n\\[ 10 \\times 9 = 90 \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the probability that the same two red candies are both picked by Terry and Mary:**\n\\[ \\frac{90}{380} \\]\n\n6. **Add the probabilities of Terry picking two blue candies and two red candies:**\n\\[ \\frac{90}{380} + \\frac{90}{380} = \\frac{180}{380} = \\frac{9}{19} \\]\n\n7. **Convert the fraction to its irreducible form:**\n\\[ \\frac{9}{19} \\]\n\n8. **Sum the numerator and the denominator:**\n\\[ m+n = 9 + 19 = 28 \\]\n\n#### Final Answer:\n\\[ \\boxed{28} \\]",
